attempts.prompt:
Make a strictly LOCALIZED content-and-lettering edit to this Orsugal character folio. Preserve its successful Canadian Group of Seven observational oil treatment, matte painted surfaces, broad connected colour/value masses, gentle diffuse daylight, exact overall layout, every dragon's identity, anatomy, scale, pose and colours. Do not restyle, redraw or polish unaffected areas.

1. Remove ONLY these decorative prose/motto text blocks, wherever they appear, and paint the vacated areas quiet matte ivory matching their immediate surroundings:
“OBSERVE / SIMPLIFY / GROUP / PAINT” at upper left;
“Ancient mind. / Modest size. / Same sky.” at upper right;
“Lean. Ancient. / Observant. / Slightly disgruntled. / Always himself.” below the main state label;
“Once among / the big hills.” at lower left;
“Same spirit. / Smaller tasks.” below the lodge;
“PLACES ENDURE. / SO DO WE.” at lower right.
Remove the little decorative dash below each removed text block as well. Keep the identifying heading “ORSUGAL”, exact subtitle “A Beginner of Considerable Age”, “ADVENTURER — HOUND-SIZED”, useful lateral/rear view captions, head study caption, foreclaw/acorn caption, “BEFORE ENROLMENT — GIANT” and “THE LODGE” intact, readable and unchanged. Add no text.

2. In the lower-right lodge vignette ONLY, replace the silver bucket-like vessel hanging from the dragon's mouth with a plain silver festival drinking cup: open cup rim, modest foot, and exactly ONE ordinary side loop handle. The dragon grips that SIDE LOOP in his teeth. NO top carry bail, arch over the rim, bucket or lidded tankard. Keep the cup ordinary human-cup size, the dragon's head/pose unchanged, and the matte broad-brush daylight painting consistent with the rest of the vignette.

3. In the upper-right head study ONLY, keep the tiny candle-sized flame, with a small warm yellow base and an unmistakably BLUE tip. No glow on the dragon or background, no spotlight and no enlarged flame.

Everything else remains unchanged, especially the four legs plus two separate wings, pale throat, bronze-brown body, mature facial identity, horns, quiet ivory ground, two distinct chronological size states, orchard and lodge scenery. This is a small corrective edit, not a new composition.
